import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'endgame':('Endgame: last uniques, recalling from depth 65','A Warrior with a Word of Recall scroll recalls from depth 65 while hunting a unique at that depth; its deepest level reached is 99 and fewer than five uniques are still alive. The branch comment says to reset the recall depth (cleaning up the last uniques for the Morgoth push). The original answers the game\'s "Set recall depth?" prompt with n, against its own comment; the correction answers y.'),
 'generic':('Control: generic reset branch (deepest level 60)','The same geometry with the deepest level reached at 60, so the generic reset branch runs instead. Both versions answer y and the complete logs are byte-identical.'),
 'mismatch':('Control: hunted unique far from here','With the hunted unique far from the current depth, the branch that declines to touch recall depth runs. Both versions answer n and the complete logs are byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/recalldepth-310 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('SETUP maxdepth=','setup'),('DECISION ','decision'),('OUTCOME ','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  seq=re.search(r'sequence=(.*)',raw)
  entry['sequence']=seq[1].strip() if seq else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The endgame recall-depth answer contradicted its own comment</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native recall-depth answers</p><h1>The endgame recall answer contradicted its own comment</h1><p>When the Borg recalls while hunting the last uniques before Morgoth, the game asks "Set recall depth to current depth?" The branch's comment says to reset the depth — that is what cleans up the remaining uniques — but the code answered n with a note saying "Not Resetting recall depth." The correction restores the answer the comment describes, and removes the stale half-comment about saving potions that came in with the changed key.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The situation</button><button data-step="1">The answer</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>The generic reset branch (deepest level 60) and the hunted-depth mismatch branch both keep their answers — y and n respectively — with byte-identical logs, so the correction changes only the endgame branch.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior, depth 65 (declared), seed 1000, glowing constructed arena, a known Word of Recall scroll in the pack, full hp, borg traits and unique-tracking state set directly. The production recall attempt queues its keys; they are shown, not executed in the game. This isolates the endgame branch answer, not full autonomous play; no survival or progress claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/310">issue310</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}
function answerLabel(c){if(!c||!c.outcome)return'?';return c.outcome.reset_y?'Answers y (reset depth)':(c.outcome.keep_n?'Answers n (keep depth)':'No prompt answered')}
function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`Deepest ${d.setup?d.setup.maxdepth:'?'}, current ${d.setup?d.setup.curdepth:'?'}, hunted ${d.setup?d.setup.hunted:'?'}.`:`${answerLabel(d)}`;p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'The Borg reads a Word of Recall and the game asks about recall depth.':'The queued answer key.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===1?`Queued: ${d.sequence||'none'}`:'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}
document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='endgame'?'The original answers n against its own comment; the correction answers y and resets the depth.':'Both versions agree in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}
select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
